Disables 256-bit global load/store vectorization on Blackwell (sm_100+) to support older ptxas versions (such as PTXAS 8.7 in CUDA 12.8).

On Blackwell architectures with PTX 8.8+, upstream Triton generates 256-bit global memory load and store instructions (e.g. ld.global.v8.b32, st.global.v8.b32, ld.global.v4.b64). Older ptxas toolchains fail to compile these 256-bit vector memory instructions. Capping maxVecBits at 128 bits avoids ptxas compilation failures and allows compilation with older toolchains.

